rise of the Tomb Raider is doubling down  on skills so players can customize Lara  to their play style whether it's taking  down multiple enemies at once crafting  new weapons or learning languages  there's a lot of new abilities we  haven't seen before so we talked to game  director Brian Horton to go in-depth on  some of the new skills for adventuring  hunting and combat we broken skills down  into three separate categories in the  last game we had categories but you had  to unlock them in such a way that didn't  really give you the choice on which area  you would invest in you'd have to sort  of do them all universally now we're  giving you choices so for instance if  you're a more aggressive player the  brawler category might be great for you  and what we do is we use our skill  points which you earn in game two to  unlock certain abilities and one of our  favorite abilities is definite above the  native sets snares in the clearing  must-have plan for us to pursue  beginning of the game when you climb up  a tree you're prompted to knock a guy  out from above this is a multi-stage  process you jump down it knocks them on  the ground and you have to pick up a  rock and take them out this is both slow  and also a little bit loud not perfect  for stealth so when you achieve this  upgrade you're able to use your knife  and do a death from above in one single  shot it's more stealthy and it's a great  move to really show her escalation and  power and ability to stay silent  predator  second category is the hunter category  this helps with Lara's hunting and  scavenging abilities now one of our  favorites in this area is the double  shot this allows Lara to line up two  targets in one pull and get to reticles  that form over those targets and release  kills both targets in one shot the third  category is survivor this is crafting an  exploration so one of our favorite  skills for this is the body trap  specialist what this allows you to do is  take one of the bombs that you've  crafted assign it to one of the corpses  in the game this sends out a ping in the  world enemies will be gravitated toward  this ping as soon as they get in  proximity the poison gas will go off in  an area effect this takes out multiple  enemies in one shot it's extremely  satisfying to pull off  you hear that  there's more to our skills than just  combat centric abilities and upgrades we  also have these skills that really help  you for if you're an explorer if you  really like to collect a hundred percent  of everything in the game we have one  called I for detail and that allows you  to illuminate things challenge objects  everything in the world that you might  want to collect and gives that player an  ability to really get a hundred percent  of the items that we have to offer in  the game illuminates them gives you an  idea of where to find them so it's great  for that but ultimately Lara in her  heart is an archaeologist she's someone  who loves to explore these ancient  spaces and in doing so we wanted to  improve on some of the systems that  embrace that part of a personality and  that's where our language system came  into place there's going to be model us  all throughout the world that Lara will  have to decipher in different languages  she first encounters one that's in Greek  in the Syrian tomb and she'll be able to  decipher these by going up to murals  reading journals using that as an  ability to build her language skill and  ultimately translate these model lists  the model lists are great because once  you translate them they give you  locations all throughout the world that  you'll be able to collect things like  such as gold coins that we use later on  in the game that you'll be able to trade  for more powerful weapons or a new  outfit that the player might want to  collect so these is a really cool  economy and also just feeds into the  idea of what Lara is all about which is  being this archaeologist this person  that discovers these ancient locations  we'll have to wait until November 10th  to see how deep Lara's skill  customizations go and how much they  influence individual play style check  back with us later this week when we're  going to go in-depth on creating Lara's  character and the new worlds you'll be  exploring in her latest adventure
 

